course: dictionary
lesson: 14297
title: Nourishment: food and growth
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Nourishment is the food and the good things in it that living things need to live, grow and stay healthy. Read the words around it to find its meaning. «Plants get nourishment from soil, water and sunlight.» Plants cannot eat like we do, so the sentence tells you that nourishment is what they need to grow.
explain: «Babies get all their nourishment from milk.» Milk is food, so nourishment means food and the good things inside it. Check by swapping the word in: "Babies get all their food from milk" still makes sense, so your meaning is right.
explain: Nourishment can also feed your mind. «Reading every day is nourishment for the mind.» Books do not fill your stomach, but they help your thinking and feelings grow, so this is the second meaning: something that helps your mind grow.
fact: Nourishment is a noun, and it is uncountable: you say some nourishment, not a nourishment.
fact: «Nourishment» means food and the good things in it that living things need to live, grow and stay healthy.
fact: Useful phrases are "get nourishment from" and "source of nourishment".
fact: «A source of nourishment» is something that gives you food or helps you grow, like milk for babies or sunlight for plants.
fact: Something that helps your mind or feelings grow can also be called nourishment for the mind.
exercise: «Plants get nourishment from soil, water and sunlight.» What does nourishment mean here? | Pots and gardening tools | A kind of soil | Sunny days and warm weather | *Food and the good things that help a plant live and grow
exercise: «Reading every day is nourishment for the mind.» What is the mind being given? | Food to eat | *Something that helps it grow | Noise | Sleep
exercise: Copy the word from this sentence that means food and the good things in it: «Vegetables give your body good nourishment.» | vegetables | body | *nourishment | good
test: Lily says nourishment is just a fancy word for sweets. Why is she wrong? | *Nourishment is the food and good things that living things need to grow | Sweets are the best nourishment for every body | Nourishment is only for animals | Nourishment means the same as treats
test: Which sentence uses nourishment correctly? | Our dog ran nourishment across the park | Nourishment is a very loud noise | Please give me three nourishments for lunch | *Good nourishment, like fruit and vegetables, helps children grow strong
exam: Why do children need nourishment? | *It gives them what they need to grow and stay healthy | It makes them taller in a single day | It means they will never feel tired at school | Only plants need nourishment
